a sequence \{x}{\cf2\fs16\dn n}{\cf2 , n=0,...,J-1\}, we can define a }{
\cf2\b nd-delayed version}{\cf2  of the sequence by prefixing it with 
nd zeros. The delayed sequence therefore has length J+nd. Of course, 
we can postfix the delayed sequence with zeros to define a sequence of 
longer length N. We can implement this in Mathcad as follows.}}
