\plain\cf1\fs20 \pard {\cf2\f1\fs24\b Example 2.2 
_____________________________________}{\cf2\b  \par }{\cf2 We compute 
a simple example of the periodic convolution that evidences the cyclic 
or wrap around effect for appropriate choice of parameters. The FIR is 
of length M+1 and we are given an input signal of length J. We wish to 
compute the periodic convolution with period N. We assume M<J<N. }{\cf2
\b  }}
